{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Shape 3 confirmed as a real, uncovered gap — the other two shapes are not\n\nMeasured against `origin/main` at `eba93991965`.\n\n**The rubric says nothing about LOC bounds.** `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-tests.md`\nis 130 lines; `grep -n \"LOC\\|line count\\|module size\\|ceiling\\|floor\"` over it returns no\nmatch (RC=1). So a new test that hard-codes an upper LOC bound on a `src/rebar` file draws\nno finding from the tests criterion today.\n\n**ADR 0058 forbids exactly that.** `docs/adr/0058-the-module-size-limit-file-is-the-only-loc-ceiling.md:26-29`:\n\"`.github/module-size-limit.txt` is the single authoritative LOC ceiling... No other test\nmay assert an upper LOC bound on a `src/rebar` file, and none may hard-code a ceiling\nvalue.\" The ADR also preserves the anti-fragmentation FLOOR (`:31-37`) as explicitly NOT\ncovered by the prohibition, so a taxonomy that treats \"LOC pinning\" as one undifferentiated\nshape would wrongly flag the floor.\n\nThat is a standing project decision with no enforcement in the review path -- the gap this\nticket is actually about.\n\n**The other two shapes in this description do not survive re-measurement**, per the\nexisting cross-reference comment: the held-out-twin premise names a convention retired\noutright by `0b5d004f394` (0 tracked files match `heldout`/`held_out`, epic `6ed2-24e5`\nclosed), and the ~30 lint-rerunning modules are currently BLESSED by the rubric's guard\n(iii) plus the Rule-5 structural-artifact exception, making that a change in the rubric's\njudgement rather than a coverage gap.\n\n**Consequence for scope.** This ticket is rescopable rather than obsolete, but to one\nnarrow shape: teach the tests criterion that a test asserting an upper LOC bound on a\n`src/rebar` file, or hard-coding a ceiling value, is a finding -- while explicitly exempting\nthe anti-fragmentation floor and `test_module_size_contract.py`, which ADR 0058 names as the\nsingle sanctioned mirror. The description's RED PROOF must also replay a guard diff from\ngit history (e.g. `git show b91f8f6830c`), since all 5 named guard modules are deleted."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793701070427436001,"uuid":"7271e1f9-57ad-4c80-aee0-c6c42a73ab61"}